Z||000002||stimpy||02-07-2000||07:58 PM||||I believe a good running V6 Fiero should go no lower than $1600. I suggest that you clean the paint up,a shiny car is a more expensive car in many a buyers perception. I would be happy to provide pointers on how to properly wet-sand a car to get that mirror finish. Email me and I will reply with all the materials you would need for a proper job.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-07-2000||08:02 PM||||stimpy has a good point about shining the car.  While you're at it you should make sure the interior is as clean as possible (shampoo the carpet, use deodorizer if you're a smoker, etc.) and scrub the wheels, tires, engine bay, etc too.  Also, unless something such as a pedal cover is missing or totally destroyed, I wouldn't suggest replacing it.  Some people would think that a brand new pedal cover might indicate that you are trying to cover something up.||||reg||1
